WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.956
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Fairness Check.

00:00:12.956 --> 00:00:17.913
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:20.886
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:23.860
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:30.799
Sometimes something happens in our classroom, and a feeling rises up fast: "That's not fair!"

00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:38.729
That feeling is real. It is allowed. And it deserves a closer look before it grows.

00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:47.651
Here is something true: fair does not always mean the same. Different people need different things.

00:00:47.651 --> 00:00:51.616
When that feeling rises, we can run a little check. It has three questions.

00:00:51.616 --> 00:00:59.546
Question one: What happened? Just the plain facts, like telling a story.

00:00:59.546 --> 00:01:08.467
Question two: What did each person need? Needs are not all the same size.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:18.380
One friend might need extra time. Another might need a quiet corner. Another might need a tool that helps their hands or their eyes.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:26.310
Question three: If I needed that, would it feel fair to me? Put yourself in their chair and look again.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.301
Three questions. That is the whole check.

00:01:27.301 --> 00:01:36.223
A classmate getting what they need is not something taken from you. Nothing leaves your desk when a friend gets help.

00:01:36.223 --> 00:01:45.144
And nobody's need is your business to announce. The check is for your own heart, not for telling the class.

00:01:45.144 --> 00:01:52.083
Sometimes the check shows things really are uneven — and then you can say so, calmly, to a grown-up.

00:01:52.083 --> 00:01:53.074
The feeling was never wrong. The check just helps it see clearly.

00:01:53.074 --> 00:02:00.013
What happened. What did each person need. Would it feel fair if I needed that?

00:02:00.013 --> 00:02:04.970
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.935
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:08.935 --> 00:02:13.891
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:13.891 --> 00:02:18.847
You're ready for what's next.
